<title>USA: Centerior Ohio nuke at 40 pct and rising.</title>
<headline>Centerior Ohio nuke at 40 pct and rising.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Centerior Energy Corp's 877 megawatt Davis Besse nuclear power unit was operating at 40 percent of capacity early this morning and increasing power, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Thursday.</p>
<p>The unit, in Oak Harbor, Ohio, had been reduced to 10 percent power Wednesday &quot;due to failure to perform vacuum leak testing on the decay heat pit inspection cover,&quot; the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>The unit was placed back on line early this morning.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
